
title: Paper
---
<<declare $takenPaper = false>>

There's a piece of paper on the floor. Do you take it?

-> \[ACTION\] Take it.
    <<jump PaperTaken>>
-> \[ACTION\] Crumple it up and take it.
    <<jump PaperCrumple>>
-> Leave
    <<stop>>
===
title: PaperTaken
---
<<useAction>>
<<PaperTook>>
<<set $takenPaper = true>>
You take the paper and carefully stow it away in your backpack.
<<stop>>
===
title: PaperCrumple
---
<<useAction>>
<<PaperCrumpleTook>>
<<set $takenPaper = true>>
You grab the paper and crumple it and stuff it into your pocket.
<<stop>>
===


title: Evidence
---
<<if getBool("hasEvidence")>>
    Nothing else to see here.
    <<stop>>
<<else>>
    Looking into the desk, you find a file named Chaplain. Inside it shows he has 0 credits!

    -> \[ACTION\] Take the files.
        <<setBool "hasEvidence" true>>
        <<useAction>>
    -> Don't take it.
        <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===

title: LastCredit
---
Looks like Willie dropped a credit, probably one he got from a skipper.

-> \[ACTION\] Take the credit.
    <<CreditTaken>>
    <<GotCredit>>
    <<useAction>>
    <<jump EndOfDay>>
-> Don't take it.
    <<stop>>
===

title: Speaker
---
Steal the speaker? 
-> \[ACTION\] Yes
    <<jump steal>>
-> Nah
   <<stop>>
<<stop>>
===

title: steal
---
<<if getBool("samGettingBall")>>
    You take the speaker
    <<setBool "speakerStolen" true>>
    <<removeSpeaker>>
    <<useAction>>
<<else>>
    Sam: WHAT ARE YOU DOING!?
    <<gameOver "If you want his speaker, you need to take it in secret.">>
<<endif>>
===